# Database Configuration
# For development, use a local PostgreSQL instance
# For production, use DanubeDB PostgreSQL (EU region only)

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/budget_planner

# DanubeData Production Database (story 4.17).
# Used here by packages/db/drizzle.config.ts, which loads THIS file via dotenv to
# run `db:migrate` locally. In production nothing reads a .env file — every value
# below is injected as a Rapids secret (see docs/production-database-runbook.md).
#
# The managed instance is reachable only over DanubeData internal DNS. The host
# must satisfy `isEuSovereignDbHost` in packages/db/src/client.ts: a dot-anchored
# `.danubedata.com` host, or the internal writer name by exact match.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@budget-planner-prod-rw:5432/budget-planner

# CA certificate (PEM) for the managed instance's TLS chain. Read directly from
# process.env by packages/db/src/client.ts; it is not part of the Zod env schema.
# DATABASE_CA_CERT=

# Application environment. `production` arms every fail-closed path (EU host
# allowlist, TLS verification, SESSION_SECRET floor). Unset is treated as
# production-grade, not as development.
# NODE_ENV=production

# Session signing secret (HMAC-SHA256 key for signed session cookies).
# REQUIRED in production (NODE_ENV=production): the app fails to authenticate
# anyone if this is missing or shorter than 32 characters. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Rotating this value invalidates all existing sessions (users must re-login).
# In development it may be omitted (an insecure fallback is used with a warning).
SESSION_SECRET=
